  "notStated": {
    "undocumentedFlagBits": "Bits 3 and 5 of the flag register are called not used and given no behaviour. What the part actually drives them with is settled by the recording alone.",
    "internalRegisterWZ": "The manual never mentions the internal register the recording calls WZ, which two instructions copy their undocumented flag bits from. Every claim this project makes about it rests on the recording.",
    "flagsModifiedLatch": "The manual never mentions the latch the recording calls Q, which records whether the instruction just executed wrote the flags. Same footing as WZ.",
    "internalCyclePlacement": "The manual gives how many T states each machine cycle takes and how many machine cycles an instruction has. It does not say, for a machine cycle longer than its bus access needs, where within that cycle the bus is idle. A cycle-by-cycle model needs that ordering and has to take it from the recording.",
    "undocumentedOpcodes": "The manual describes the documented instruction set. The prefixed forms that reach the halves of the index registers, and the ED opcodes that are not listed, are not in it at all."
  }
